  (no_connect (at 147.32 187.96) (uuid 59799c52-dbf4-5d79-80dc-1ad03308c2ee))
  (no_connect (at 50.8 63.5) (uuid 4b27a5de-1436-5423-a786-e24d738f8f32))
  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nA LONE NO-CONNECT PIN'S NET IS NAMED AFTER THE PIN (the export names it so, whatever label it carries), so the\none-pin nets the text below names are, on this sheet: ON_DIVIDER is NO.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity.\n\nTHIS CIRCUIT IS DRAWN ON ANOTHER PAGE. The load switch sits inside power-entry.md's entry drawing,\ndeliberately, because that is one board and one drawing; this page carries only the gate-network detail. So\nthe labels that describe these parts are on a page whose netlist does not own them - which is why\ntools/check-netlist.py resolves a drawing label against EVERY netlist, not just the one beside the page.\nBefore that, every load-switch label on power-entry.md was skipped as \"a BOM row, not a component here\" and\nits value was never compared to anything.\n\n[pins] quoted: YAML reads a bare ON as true\n\n[note] NO `value:` ON PURPOSE. The row is open and says the value is selected on the bench at E6 with a\ncurrent probe, because the +-11% window the page wants is narrower than the LT1641's own sense-threshold\ntolerance. The 50 mohm in power-entry.md's drawing is the WORKING figure the 0.940 A limit is computed from,\nnot a chosen part.\n\n[note] NO `value:` - the part is not chosen, and the single-pulse SOA curve at V_DS = 12 V decides it, not\nR_DS(on).\n\n[pins] quoted: YAML reads a bare NO as false\n\n[SENSE_NODE] The sense resistor's far end IS the FET drain, and the pin that watches it.\n\n[GATE_COMP_MID] R-GATE-COMP and C-GATE in SERIES to ground. The series pair is the compensation zero; the\ncapacitor alone is not.\n\n['ON'] quoted: YAML reads a bare ON as true\n\n['NO'] THE UNDERVOLTAGE-LOCKOUT DIVIDER IS NOT DESIGNED, and the page says so. ON is a threshold input, not a\nswitch input: it needs a divider from the rail so the part knows the supply is up, and the toggle interrupts\nor pulls that divider. Until the divider exists there is nothing to say the switch's second terminal lands on.\n\n[PWRGD] PWRGD IS NOT USED. The presence detect that would have read it is deleted, and the panel indicator's\n\"latched\" signal is proposed only - the Interfaces table marks TIMER/GATE the same way, with nothing drawn." (at 408.94 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 3e09ec79-e312-5333-a8e2-c8aea047f8bf))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
